  "content": {
    "body": "Every pebble type has its OWN extraction standard, below. The BAR is the\nsame for all: capture EVERYTHING the source shows, invent nothing,\ndescribe and status every unit, code-link the sources you read, reconcile\ncounts, and mark any partial capture as partial — never present a subset\nas the whole. CLASSIFY first, then follow that type's standard exactly.\n\n## model — a persisted table\nTruth is the STORAGE, never the ORM's convenience. Read the schema:\nmigrations, the DDL, a schema dump, or raw SQL — this works even when\nthere is NO ORM. WALK THE FULL MIGRATION HISTORY for the table: the\ncurrent shape is the SUM of every create/add-column/rename/type-change/\ndrop/index change (a column added in migration 12 and renamed in 30\nreflects 30). Capture EVERY column — timestamps, soft-deletes, audit and\nflag columns included (boring columns are columns): name, DB type,\nrequired (= NOT NULL), default verbatim, primaryKey, plus the constraints\nthat are also spec (uniques, composite/covering indexes, check\nconstraints, enum values, casts, generated/virtual columns, JSON/array/\npolymorphic columns captured with a note). SECOND PASS for relationships:\nevery FK / *_id column whose target model pebble exists gets\nrefKey {path, field}; name the unlinked ones and why. RECONCILE: the table\nhas N columns, the pebble shows N fields, or you state the gap.\n\n## structure — an in-code shape (DTO / payload / config / return type)\nTruth is the source code. Code types (string, number, SomeClass); NO DB\nsemantics (no primaryKey/refKey/NOT NULL/defaults). Capture every field —\noptionals, unions, enums, nested shapes; nest other models/structures via\ntypeRef instead of redefining them.\n\n## contract — a wire surface (endpoint / event / webhook)\nCapture every route/event: method, path, status codes, auth and header\nrequirements (in descriptions). Request and response PAYLOADS reference\nstructures via typeRef — never redefined inline. Document EVERY outcome\nthe surface promises (each status code / error shape), not just the happy\nresponse.\n\n## requirement / checklist\nOne item per verifiable behavior the code ACTUALLY exhibits — each with a\ntestable description (\"given X, when Y, then Z\"). Only what the code does;\nnothing aspirational. Capture every behavior found, not a sample.\n\n## test — a test plan\nOne item per real test case found in the test files, each with the status\nits latest run shows (pass → verified, fail → broken, none → planned).\nLink the test files; capture every case, including the negative/edge ones.\n\n## architecture\nThe real topology from the dependency graph: components (services, apps,\nmodules, datastores, queues) and the dependencies the code ACTUALLY wires\nbetween them — cite the import/call edges. Capture allowed vs present\nedges truthfully; never draw a dependency the code doesn't have.\n\n## knowledge\nDocument a topic/subsystem from the REAL code — how it actually works, its\nconcepts and moving parts — with each claim cited to file:line. No\ninvention, no aspiration; if something isn't in the code, it isn't in the\ndoc.\n\n## agent / skill / memory (authored types)\nThese are AUTHORED, not derived from code. \"Extraction\" here means\ncapturing an EXISTING one faithfully and completely (a persona from\nconfig, a command/script from a harness folder, a durable fact from a\nsession): record its real role / steps / tools / boundaries / content —\nevery required field real and described, none left filler.\n\n## always (every type)\nFill via update with the FULL content (the CLI rejects a field missing a\ndescription or status); link-code every source file you read; set status\nimplemented per unit (verified only with proven behavior); reconcile and\nreport what you captured and what remains.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-21T14:32:38.673Z",
  "description": "The self-contained extraction standard for each pebble type. One shared bar — capture EVERYTHING the source shows, invent nothing, describe + status every unit, code-link sources, reconcile counts — with a method defined natively per type.",
